    "instruction_fr": "Cette version utilise une file simple : elle fixe la première distance trouvée, pas la plus courte. Corrige-la avec heapq.",
    "starter_code": "from collections import deque\n\ndef dijkstra(graphe, depart):\n    dist = {depart: 0}\n    file = deque([depart])\n    while file:\n        ville = file.popleft()\n        for voisin, km in graphe[ville].items():\n            if voisin not in dist:\n                dist[voisin] = dist[ville] + km\n                file.append(voisin)\n    return dist\n",
    "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef dijkstra(graphe, depart):\n    dist = {depart: 0}\n    tas = [(0, depart)]\n    while tas:\n        d, ville = heapq.heappop(tas)\n        if d > dist[ville]:\n            continue\n        for voisin, km in graphe[ville].items():\n            nouvelle = d + km\n            if voisin not in dist or nouvelle < dist[voisin]:\n                dist[voisin] = nouvelle\n                heapq.heappush(tas, (nouvelle, voisin))\n    return dist\n",
